(ns arbace.j2g.start
  "The classes initialized at start (Futamura F4, doc/FUTAMURA-SURVEY.md, \"F4 and F2's j2g
  fixes as built\"): the runtime's classes that the program initializes before any user code,
  by their Go names (package path, a dot, the Go type name), in the order it initializes them.
  In compiled code (arbace.c2j's classes) j2g omits their initialization guard: their static
  methods are called through guard-free entries (C_m_NoInit), their statics read and written
  unguarded. The first compiled code initializes those whose initialization has not started
  yet, in this order, and stops the program when one is still not started (jrt.StartCheck).
  Generated by test/j2g/start_classes.ae from the program's ARBACE_TRACE_INIT runs; do not
  edit.")

(def classes
  "The Go names of the classes initialized at start, in order."
  ["arbace/jrt.Boolean"
   "arbace/jrt.Byte"
   "arbace/jrt.Character"
   "arbace/jrt.ClassNotFoundException"
